  "details": "This is something I've used to help take photos with desktop users, if I want them holding something but I don't want it floating a foot in front of them, or holding someone else's hand, its very useful to just give them an item, toggle it off for me, take the photo. Yes you can make all items invisible in camera, but that's not always what you want. For example a picture I took I wanted the desktop user holding a mug, but used the snow generator to create snowflakes falling in the background. Not everyone has VRC+ or has bought a grabbable item, and it's inconvenient to have to invite someone who does, just to take a photo. Yes desktop users can grab a personal mirror, but then they can't properly see and it's hard to pose them. \n\nWas this an often used feature? Probably not, but when you needed it, it was nice to have, and having it doesn't really take anything away from the average user",
